"{\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Rolling-origin, group-aware backtest splits.\\n\\nThe dataset is a sequence of row mappings (e.g. rows from csv.DictReader)\\nwith a time column and a group column. Time values are treated as discrete,\\nordered periods: splits operate on the sorted distinct time values (\\\"the\\ngrid\\\"), and all window sizes -- train_window, horizon, step, gap -- are\\nmeasured in grid steps, not in rows or wall-clock time. Feed in a column\\nalready bucketed to the period size you care about (e.g. an integer day\\nindex or an ISO date string) so grid steps match calendar periods.\\n\\nFold semantics, for an origin at grid position o:\\n\\n    train window : grid positions [o - train_window, o)   (sliding)\\n                   grid positions [0, o)                  (expanding)\\n    gap          : grid positions [o, o + gap) are dropped\\n    test window  : grid positions [o + gap, o + gap + horizon)\\n\\nThe first fold uses the smallest origin that satisfies the train window\\n(train_window for sliding, min_train for expanding); each subsequent origin\\nadvances by `step` grid positions. Folds stop once the test window would run\\npast the end of the grid.\\n\\nGroup awareness: the same grid cutoffs are applied to every group, so within\\na fold every group's train rows strictly precede its test rows. A group is\\nincluded in a fold only if it has at least one row in both the train and the\\ntest window; groups with too little data are omitted from that fold. A fold\\nwhere no group qualifies is skipped.\\n\\nFold rows are sorted by (time, group) and are the same dict objects as the\\ninput rows, not copies.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nfrom collections import defaultdict\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom typing import Any, Mapping, Sequence\\n\\n\\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\\nclass Fold:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"One rolling-origin fold.\\n\\n    origin     : last time value used for training (the forecast origin)\\n    test_start : first time value of the test window\\n    test_end   : last time value of the test window\\n    train/test : rows of the participating groups, sorted by (time, group)\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    index: int\\n    origin: Any\\n    test_start: Any\\n    test_end: Any\\n    train: tuple[Mapping, ...]\\n    test: tuple[Mapping, ...]\\n\\n\\ndef rolling_origin_splits(\\n    rows: Sequence[Mapping],\\n    *,\\n    time_col: str,\\n    group_col: str,\\n    horizon: int,\\n    train_window: int | None = None,\\n    step: int = 1,\\n    gap: int = 0,\\n    min_train: int = 1,\\n) -> list[Fold]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Split `rows` into rolling-origin folds.\\n\\n    Args:\\n        rows: row mappings, each containing `time_col` and `group_col`.\\n        time_col: column of mutually sortable, discrete time values.\\n        group_col: column identifying the group each row belongs to.\\n        horizon: test window length in grid steps (>= 1).\\n        train_window: training window length in grid steps; None for an\\n            expanding window that uses all history before the origin.\\n        step: origin advance per fold, in grid steps (>= 1).\\n        gap: number of grid steps dropped between train end and test\\n            start (>= 0).\\n        min_train: smallest expanding-window training length in grid steps\\n            (>= 1). Ignored when train_window is given.\\n\\n    Returns:\\n        Folds in chronological order with contiguous 0-based `index`.\\n\\n    Raises:\\n        ValueError: on invalid configuration, empty input, or an input too\\n            short to produce a single fold.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if horizon < 1:\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"horizon must be >= 1, got {horizon}\\\")\\n    if step < 1:\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"step must be >= 1, got {step}\\\")\\n    if gap < 0:\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"gap must be >= 0, got {gap}\\\")\\n    if train_window is not None and train_window < 1:\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"train_window must be >= 1 or None, got {train_window}\\\")\\n    if min_train < 1:\\n        raise ValueError(f\\\"min_train must be >= 1, got {min_train}\\\")\\n    if not rows:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"rows must not be empty\\\")\\n\\n    grid = sorted({row[time_col] for row in rows})\\n    n = len(grid)\\n    pos_of = {t: i for i, t in enumerate(grid)}\\n\\n    rows_at: dict[int, list[Mapping]] = defaultdict(list)\\n    for row in rows:\\n        rows_at[pos_of[row[time_col]]].append(row)\\n\\n    first_origin = train_window if train_window is not None else min_train\\n    if first_origin + gap + horizon > n:\\n        raise ValueError(\\n            f\\\"dataset too short: grid has {n} time steps but the first fold \\\"\\n            f\\\"needs {first_origin} train + {gap} gap + {horizon} horizon\\\"\\n        )\\n\\n    folds: list[Fold] = []\\n    origin_idx = first_origin\\n    while origin_idx + gap + horizon <= n:\\n        test_lo = origin_idx + gap\\n        train_lo = origin_idx - train_window if train_window is not None else 0\\n\\n        train_by_group: dict[Any, list[Mapping]] = defaultdict(list)\\n        for p in range(train_lo, origin_idx):\\n            for row in rows_at.get(p, ()):\\n                train_by_group[row[group_col]].append(row)\\n        test_by_group: dict[Any, list[Mapping]] = defaultdict(list)\\n        for p in range(test_lo, test_lo + horizon):\\n            for row in rows_at.get(p, ()):\\n                test_by_group[row[group_col]].append(row)\\n\\n        shared = sorted(set(train_by_group) & set(test_by_group))\\n        if not shared:\\n            origin_idx += step\\n            continue\\n\\n        key = lambda r: (r[time_col], r[group_col])\\n        train = sorted((r for g in shared for r in train_by_group[g]), key=key)\\n        test = sorted((r for g in shared for r in test_by_group[g]), key=key)\\n\\n        folds.append(Fold(\\n            index=len(folds),\\n            origin=grid[origin_idx - 1],\\n            test_start=grid[test_lo],\\n            test_end=grid[test_lo + horizon - 1],\\n            train=tuple(train),\\n            test=tuple(test),\\n        ))\\n        origin_idx += step\\n\\n    return folds\\n\",\"path\":\"splits.py\"}"